ategories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"mhrW9O0O5hXGXGnEYBVoag","name":"Jacques-Imo's Cafe","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"8KnMSrMuTI2AtHZ2LOI8OQ","name":"Maurepas Foods","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"JhpRI9m71ybWHkAqRdL0Tg","name":"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"_Bi9kN_eR75G1eqIl7S3pA","name":"The Bulldog","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"x4K6aMaOYvGhC5jhFJP2Ag","review_id":"T7eXtqV3dbTP19F1nhUomA","date":"2012-01-22T15:18:28","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9534032940864563,"text_excerpt":"Oh, yes, I'm DEFINITELY a fan of Pho Tau Bay. The service is top-notch, the food is great, and the prices can't be beat. There were four of us in this group, some Pho, some Bun, and a Bahn Mi. The service never skipped a beat. I had the Bun Thit Nuong (a rice noodle salad with grilled pork on top). The noodles were done well, the salad was fresh and crisp. The pork was a little tough, but had an excellent flavor. The egg rolls that came with it were also very good. My only fault, and it's truly a minor one, is I've found I'm NOT a fan of Jasmine tea and that's their only option for iced tea. Yeah, it's a Vietnamese restaurant, but you're also in one of the iced-tea-capitals of the South. ..."},{"business_id":"x4K6aMaOYvGhC5jhFJP2Ag","review_id":"fBeyyj4pOEYQF83hNQoMCA","date":"2012-04-27T17:46:23","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9487169981002808,"text_excerpt":"I am a newbie when it comes to Vietnamese food. In fact, I tried it for the first time with a friend Uptown a few days ago. The next day I was headed to Subway for lunch when I remembered much another friend liked Pho Tau Bay. I quickly changed my lunch plans. Located in what appears to be the oldest strip mall on the westbank, Pho Tau Bay offers very reasonably priced, great food. Since I was in a hurry, I ordered a half order of shrimp spring rolls and a pork bahn mi. The total was around $10 and I was out the door in under 10 minutes. The spring rolls were good, but something was missing. I think the large shrimp were few and far between, so most bites were just veggies. The peanut sau..."},{"business_id":"x4K6aMaOYvGhC5jhFJP2Ag","review_id":"svcIFz2Wq0FxDFItA2jqCA","date":"2011-07-11T00:34:25","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9486292600631714,"text_excerpt":"I love Pho Tau Bay. It's easily the best Vietnamese food in the metro area. The prices are reasonable and the menu is quite extensive with pho, bun, banh mi, and spring rolls. MMM... the spring rolls. Yum. Hint: If your family/dining companions can't choose one type of spring rolls, order two 1/2 portions. We end up doing this every time. Another hint: If you are dining with someone who is chopstick-challenged, you can ask for a fork. Anyway, I'm not sure what I can really write about this place that hasn't been said. The service is quick and friendly. The kitchen is fast. The food is amazing! They have desserts available by the cash register, although I haven't ever had any room left to ..."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"x4K6aMaOYvGhC5jhFJP2Ag","photo_id":"yD5lvoEgJpTI7FihA2TAbA","label":"drink","image_url":"/photos/yD5lvoEgJpTI7FihA2TAbA.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.88499915599823},{"business_id":"x4K6aMaOYvGhC5jhFJP2Ag","photo_id":"dYoL1sxS_ZAzd5jSAfKRYQ","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/dYoL1sxS_ZAzd5jSAfKRYQ.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8494267463684082},{"business_id":"x4K6aMaOYvGhC5jhFJP2Ag","photo_id":"kFnMxHsS